        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: the event-level review remains incomplete\n\nI verified the relevant work order and September Pending Close cutoff, but the authorized records contain **no cost-event rows**. The supporting event records are restricted to the records-custodian role, so I cannot substantiate the transaction-specific details or conclude whether a late event occurred.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, DeKoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Not available in authorized evidence |\n| Event amount | Not available in authorized evidence |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available in authorized evidence |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available in authorized evidence |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Cannot determine** without the event type, creation time, and recorded status |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly as stored; no timezone or UTC offset was supplied.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation states that new transactions falling in or before a **Pending Close** period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing after Pending Close.**\n\n*Source: “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233, printed page 225.*\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary manufacturing transaction newly created after the cutoff should be held from staging/processing. **Whether this event’s recorded status follows that rule remains unverified—not a finding that no late event exists.**\n\nI requested an authorized release of the missing evidence. No database records were changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_f6325e7b5332/audit-report.json`\n\nThe submitted report is marked **needs_evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
